{
    "metadata": {
        "schema_version": "1.0",
        "title": "Test fixture: what an ATC subgroup's own published NAME licenses (issues #183, #184)",
        "note": "Rows copied field-for-field from the 19 MB openmrs-ddi-knowledge-base DDInter 2.0 dataset, in KB order, with interactions emptied so every assertion here is about contraindication chip TEXT. One pair per limb of the criterion: Chloramphenicol/Gentamicin share only purpose-headed subgroups (S01AA Antibiotics, S02AA/S03AA Antiinfectives) and no chemistry; Rifampicin/Capreomycin share only J04AB Antibiotics, which is purpose-headed and NOT inside a locally applied group; Eliglustat/Givosiran and Miglustat/Eliglustat share only A16AX, a residue whose ancestry is residue all the way to the anatomical main group. The controls: Ampicillin/Amoxicillin share J01CA (Penicillins with extended spectrum), Gentamicin/Tobramycin share J01GB (Other aminoglycosides, a residue under a chemically named parent), Loratadine/Ketotifen share R06AX (a residue under ANTIHISTAMINES FOR SYSTEMIC USE, a mechanism), and Fluorometholone/Dexamethasone share S01BA/C05AA (Corticosteroids) inside locally applied groups - all four name chemistry or a molecular target and keep their claim. Miconazole/Clotrimazole share A01AB (purpose-named, sorts first), D01AC and G01AF (both imidazole-derivative subgroups): the one pair shape where the two arms name DIFFERENT classes, because their candidate sets differ while the preference between candidates does not."
    },
